   "project": "ledgerlite",
   "reply": "The tests now pass with your original command, `python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`. Both tests in `tests/test_ledger.py` run and pass.\n\nThere were two problems:\n1. **No package marker:** `tests/` had no `__init__.py`, so `-t .` rejected it as a start directory. I added an `__init__.py`.\n2. **Import path:** the code lives under `src/ledgerlite`, which isn't on the import path, so `from ledgerlite import Ledger` failed. The new `tests/__init__.py` also puts `src/` on `sys.path`.\n\nThe only change is the new file `tests/__init__.py`. Installing the package, for example with `pip install -e .`, would also fix the import. The project has no packaging config, so I used the path approach.",
